    <h2 class="mt-4">Offers &amp; pricing</h2>
    <div class="faq" data-schema="true">
      <details><summary>How much will you offer me?</summary><p>For a cash purchase, typically 75–85% of open-market value. For an assisted sale, often closer to full market value once we refurbish and sell. For tenanted property, we price on yield — usually 11–14x annual net rent. Exact figures depend on condition, area, situation, and route.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Why aren't your cash offers 100% of market value?</summary><p>Because we're carrying the cost, risk, and timeline. A 100% offer in cash with a 14-day completion isn't a real offer — anyone making it is either lying or planning to renegotiate at the last minute. We'd rather give you an honest figure you can rely on.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Can I negotiate?</summary><p>Yes. Our first offer isn't always our best offer. If you have a counter-offer with a basis we can understand, we'll consider it. We won't move on offers where the seller's expectation is unrealistic for the route, but we'll be honest about that too.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Will you really pay all the fees?</summary><p>On a cash purchase: yes. Your conveyancing fees, Land Registration, and the Home Report are all covered. On an assisted sale, fees come out of the final sale price — they don't come out of your pocket. On other routes, fee structures vary and are agreed in writing upfront.</p></details>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-4">Timing &amp; process</h2>
    <div class="faq" data-schema="true">
      <details><summary>How fast can you complete?</summary><p>For a cash purchase, typically 14–28 days from offer accepted. Our fastest is 9 days (urgent repossession). For an assisted sale, you receive your share once the refurb completes and sells — usually 8–16 weeks.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Why can't you complete in 3 days like some sites advertise?</summary><p>Because Scottish missives take time, Land Register takes time, AML checks take time, and your solicitor needs days to do their work properly. Any cash buyer advertising 3-day completion is misrepresenting the legal process.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Do I need to be in Scotland to sell?</summary><p>No. Many sellers are in England or abroad. Scottish solicitors can act remotely. Signing can be done by post, online witness, or video appointment.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Do I need a solicitor?</summary><p>Yes. Scottish property law requires solicitor involvement on both sides. We pay your reasonable conveyancing fees on a cash purchase. We can recommend solicitors we've worked with if you don't have one.</p></details>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-4">Specific situations</h2>
    <div class="faq" data-schema="true">
      <details><summary>Will you buy a property that needs major work?</summary><p>Yes — that's exactly the type of property our <a href="/solutions/assisted-sale.php">assisted sale</a> route was built for. We buy damp, rewire, roof issues, full refurb, structural problems. <a href="/situations/sell-house-needing-repairs-glasgow.php">See properties needing repairs</a>.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Will you buy a property with tenants?</summary><p>Yes, regularly. Tenants stay where they are. PRT, deposits, EPC obligations all transfer to us. <a href="/situations/sell-tenanted-property-scotland.php">See tenanted sales</a>.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Will you buy a tenement flat with an outstanding common repair notice?</summary><p>Yes. Outstanding common repair notices, factor disputes, and unresolved scheme costs are common across Glasgow's tenement stock — particularly Govanhill, Crosshill, and parts of the Southside. We take on the obligation as new owner and factor the scheme cost into the offer rather than asking you to settle it first.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Will you buy non-standard construction?</summary><p>Yes — Wimpey No-Fines, Orlit, BISF steel-framed, prefab. Common in ex-council stock across the Central Belt. Most mortgage lenders won't touch these; we buy them as cash.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Will you help if I'm facing repossession?</summary><p>Possibly — depending on where you are in the process. <a href="/situations/avoid-repossession-glasgow.php">See our repossession page</a> for an honest breakdown of when a sale can help and when it can't.</p></details>
      <details><summary>What about inherited property still going through confirmation?</summary><p>We can value the property, agree a route in principle, and complete shortly after confirmation is granted. <a href="/situations/sell-inherited-property-glasgow.php">See inherited property</a>.</p></details>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-4">Privacy &amp; data</h2>
    <div class="faq" data-schema="true">
      <details><summary>What do you do with my data?</summary><p>We use it only to value your property and contact you about your enquiry. We don't sell, share, or pass it to third parties. See our <a href="/privacy.php">privacy policy</a>.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Will you mark my property publicly?</summary><p>No. No for-sale board, no public listing, no Rightmove ad. The sale is private until it's complete.</p></details>
